Well, which brings up a question I started to ask,
and then didn't. Some time ago, someone mentioned
that his/her survival rate had improved dramatically
with the habit of taking notes as the game was
played.

So, I started taking detailed notes, one game out
of every several.

I still don't get any closer to ascending, but I do
have this batch of stories that get written.

That's good for my creative writing skills, but then
throwing them away is painful.

Is there any point to posting them?

Example appended.

IMWTK

xanthian.

SPOILY, OF COURSE!

		  Bat Bait's Tale.

Got a wiz with a starting =oSD, might as well take a
few notes from the beginning, just in case something
good happens.

Bat Bait the Evoker St:12 Dx:18 Co:13 In:16 Wi:8 Ch:8 Chaotic
Dlvl:1 $:0 HP: 11(11) Pw:6(6) Xp:1/0 T:2

a a blessed +1 quarterstaff (weapon in hands)
b an uncursed +0 cloak of magic resistance (being worn)
i a blessed scroll of light
j an uncursed scroll of enchant armor
k an uncursed scroll of enchant weapon
l a blessed spellbook of force bolt
m an uncursed spellbook of magic missile
f a blessed potion of confusion
g an uncursed potion of restore ability
h an uncursed potion of see invisible
d an uncursed ring of shock resistance (on left hand)
e an uncursed ring of slow digestion
c a wand of striking

The two known spells suggest a combatant's role.
The potions are currently useless.
The enchant scrolls are "use immediately" ones;
the light scroll is "dip to erase" junk.
The second ring is useless.
The wand is redundant.

First steps, read both enchant scrolls, then
unweild the quarterstaff, to save a conduct. The
scrolls would be nicer blessed, but the rule in
NetHack is "use resources to survive to better
times"; right now there's no way to bless them and
their immediate use can prove lifesaving.

The opening room contains a fountain, always nice to
find early, but, as a crucial room with the stairs
up, and only 4x3, it is too small to make this the
fountain that gets broken for infinite scroll and
potion washing.

Found a scroll labeled Garven Deh, and an unlabeled,
pet approved scroll on the rest of the level,
another fountain, in a 13x5 room, that is a much
better prospect for turning into pools, in the same
room with the stairs down, also convenient.

Got to dance around Purrball I while he ate a
jackel, before he could be bothered to off a couple
of sewer rats, got down to HP:4 in the process. Oops.

Down to Dlvl:2 at T:553.

At t:600, got Wi:9. It is pretty easy to advance
that stat when low simply by searching for doors
and passages.

T:620, acquired a pet-approved clear potion.

T:776, found entrance to mines in fifth room
explored of Dlvl:2; HPs lost to rats fully
recovered. Purrball I has recently wasted a jackel
and two grid bugs, at least. Running down a hall
too fast found Bat Bait battering to death a kobold
zombie; Xp:1/1.

T: 808, got creamed by a falling rock by trap in
same room as main dungeon stairs down; recently
found another fountain in sixth room explored of
Dlvl:2.

T: 829, found an unannounced small used bookstore
shop, with one spellbook, eight scrolls, and an
obvious mimic. Bat Bait has z100 burning a hole in
his robe pocket, time for some credit cloning!

T: 1814, Bat Bait now has the contents of the shop,
a new spell, Magic Mapping, for later when more
experienced, and z2000. Unfortunately, he had to
kill a mimic from carelessly searching instead of
resting in a shop, so is now Xp:2/39, and down to
one zap left in the wand of striking.

T:2219, on Dlvl:3, aaargh! Bat Bait gets cornered by
a jackel with Purrball I nowhere in sight, is now
Xp:3/40. So much for the protection racket. Just a
bit too late, finds a lock pick and a magic whistle.
Oops, also satiated from eating that jackel. Got to
remember the ring!

T:2634, on Dlvl:4, a quick dip to Dlvl:5 yielded an
expensive camera, which back on Dlvl:4, Purrball I
approved.

T:2619, blinded by a magic trap, which spawned a
hobbit with sling and runed daggar, or perhaps two
hobbits. By lots of running around, avoided living
hobbit until Purrball I could take care of it. Bad
joss being XL:3 already, there's a floating eye on
the level. Also by luck disarmed a rolling boulder
trap before PC or pet got flattened by it.

T:2640, shifted from text-mode to tiles mode just
in time to see Purrball I become a large cat by
bashing a newt into cat kibble.

Since Dlvl:4 is now explored, and Purrball I is buff
enough, it is time to go risk Mines to improve what
is still Bat Bait's AC:8.

T:2855, back on Dlvl:2, even before entering Mines,
let Purrball deal with a rat, two grid bugs, and two
peaceful goblins, scored a pet approved +3 orcish
helm! Now AC:4, and into the Mines we go.

T:2281, for the second time in the game, Purrball I
attacks a floating eye and is frozen by its gaze.
Time to give up all hope of the protection racket
and start killing stuff, starting with that floating
eye!

T:3058, harassed by gnomes, with only a cursed
silver saber and a pet-approved runed daggar to
throw, retreated back to Dlvl:2 leaving Purrball I
frozen, when spell points ran dry. Found a
pestiferous and dangerous fox on Dlvl:2, luckily,
the runed daggar hit it and the saber killed it,
keeping the wielded weapon conduct a while longer.

Still holding onto:

Voluntary challenges:

You have been an atheist.
You have never genocided any monsters.
You have never polymorphed an object.
You have never changed form.
You have used no wishes.

That's one more than is usually easy to keep, but
not needing food prayers assists the longevity of
atheist conduct. Not that there is any hope of
keeping it anyway, I need altar help too much at
my level of playing experience.

Current status lines:

Bat Bait the Conjurer St:12 Dx:18 Co:14 In:16 Wi:9 Ch:8 Chaotic
Dlvl:2 $:2281 HP: 16(16) Pw:3(16) Xp:3/74 T:3058

Wall clock 23:00 15 Dec 2004 (-0800).

T:3255, still trying to build up Pw on Dlvl2, keep
running into riff-raff that forces chewing up spell
points as fast as they build, now at Xp:4/93,
HP:25(25), Pw:6(20). Nice HP boost!

Eventually returned to toplevel Mines, saved game.

T:3930, in toplevel Mines, several dangerous
battles, got down to HP:3, retreated around hallway
to heal. Used magic whistle to summon Purrball I
several times for needed rescue. AC improved to 2
with addition of hard shoes, which worstened force
bolt casting, but left good old "wizard's special
spell" magic missile at 0% failure. Managed a couple
of shots of magic missile through multiple opponents
in a single shot. Found nice large round shield, but
dropped it again when failure on magic missile went
up to about 56%.

T:4315, blinded by a magic trap on toplevel mines,
and as it seems to do when blinding the PC, it
summoned monsters, luckily only an iguana and a
red mold.

T:4383, toplevel Mines explored, on to Mines
2/Dlvl:4, where some dwarves and a gnome are in
sight from the stairs. Purrball immediately absorbs
a thrown dagger.

T:4408, gained a level to XP:5/174. Now HP:34(34),
Pw:14(24) (zotted a dwarf with magic missile spell).

T:4509 Tamed new pet pony Whinney I with a lichen
corpes. Bat Bait has been burdened for quite a while
from carrying 3 spellbooks. Learning is a very
weighty experience.

T:4596, Bat Bait finds a wrinkled spellbook on the
dungeon floor near the stairs, adds "Light" to his
repertoire. Since this is a dark maze level, this
spell deserves instant practice.

T:4828, our intrepid adventurer finds and disables
a rolling boulder trap on Mines 2/4.

T:4859, two quick zots of magic missile wipe out a
bunch of Gnomes, but deplete Bat Bait's spell
points. Luckily, a magic whistle and _two_ pets is
the next best thing. Pet approved dagger supply now
up to a dozen, not really using them much yet. Maybe
in Mines Town, where lighting might be better and
the daggers easier to recover, would be a good place
to get proficient at the missile weapon stuff. A
quick check shows no spells are yet enhancable.

T:5581,  in Mines Town, the biggest mess of bones
I've ever seen. One or more Hearsed bones piles,
piles of loot unattended by ghosts or tombstones,
two locally dropped bones piles, three ghosts so
far, and more junk to sort through than lifetime
to sort it out. Luckily, with now two large cats,
a large dog, and a pony as pets, perhaps they can
keep the riff-raff away while Bat Bait and I clean
up this mess. Bat Bait now has _21_ uncursed daggers
quivered, many, many more cursed ones from bones
piles sitting on the altar. Big news is an altar on
which to B/U/C ID stuff at last.  A quick check
shows the altar is unfortunately cross aligned, and
the priest still alive and well, which gives
something to do with all the gold from all these
bones piles: feed the priest's need for temple
donations. Not as fun at XL:5 as at XL:1, but Bat
Bait would never have lived to get here playing
pacifist. There's a black unicorn running around
this level too, which may soon leave Bat Bait short
of pets.

T:6074, Bat Bait still sorting goodies, found and
wearing some gray dragon scale mail, cashed in the
zorkmids on 8 points of protection, just found some
speed boots, recently advanced to XL:6, had a couple
of interesting encounters with a nymph and an
invisible Mordor Orc. Locked the pets away for a
while to protect the watch, let them back out when
a herd of rothes provided some food for the
carnivores, fed the pony the last available lichen
corpse. Current stats lines:

Bat Bait the Thaumaturge St:12 Dx:18 Co:14 In:16 Wi:11 Ch:8 Chaotic
Dlvl:5 $:295 HP:43(43) PW:18(26) AC:-15 Xp:6/417 T:6074 Satiated
Burdened

Off to fetch more bones pile stuff to the altar.

T:6133, oops, got in a fight with a Mordor orc who
had a wand, resisted magic missile twice, and then
read a scroll of Earth. I hope he's happy in there.
Bat Bait is again depleted of spell points,  still
working on hauling everything on the level to the
altar.

T:6153, at last, managed to kill a floating eye that
dropped a corpse and with the pets again locked
away, gained a strange mental acuity. Now to go find
that blindfold in all the ruck on the altar.

T:6466, just realized that stupid Mordor orc with
his Earth scroll and wand (of fire, from the damage
it did to a cloak) killed the watch captain, making
it safe to let the pets, who can handle the Watch
regulars, out of stir to do battle again. Got an
_uncursed_ sliver saber, though without two-weapon,
that's not as useful to a wizard as to many, from
the watch captain's effects.

T:6595, all of the watch are dead, the shopkeepers
are still alive and the shops unplundered. The prior
adventurers had a rough go of it. Use of a blindfold
shows that the stupid Mordor orc is still alive
under the central boulder of the ones he summoned,
they must be a tough breed. Bat Bait got a pair of
what must be plain leather gloves off one of the
watch, plain since they don't interfere with
spellcasting, and so is now AC:-16. There are still
some monsters in an unexplored (right hand side)
part of Mines Town, which must also be where the
stairs down are sitting. Just a little more cruft
to clear out of the rest of the level, then off to
get rid of that crowd, then Bat Bait must attempt
some scamming of the several surviving shopkeepers.
Despite eating next to nothing, the status line
keeps showing "Satiated", but Wi:11 is current, so
searching must be outbalancing bad eating habits
in terms of which way wisdom gets exercised. The
co-aligned unicorn is still alive, rather
surprisingly, and for the same reason, that they
haven't gotten in a fight with it yet, so are all
four pets. One more large dog couldn't be salvaged
when first entering this level, due to lack of food
to tame it.

A _really_ nice plan would be to clear the level,
break a fountain now that there's no watch to remark
on the deed, dip some of the masses of cursed
potions in the resulting pool, find a junk or
duplicate spellbook, dip it, and write and read a
spellbook of identify. There is just too much
"stuff" here not to want to know what all of it is,
but far too much to lift for a lucky full identify,
it would perhaps take 5 or 10 of them to get it all.

T:7440, tamed a fifth pet, pony Whinney II. Recently
advanced to XL:7, bankrupted and emptied all four
shops in Mines Town, traded in gold for one more
point of AC protection and one "thanks for the
selfless generosity" Grrr. Anyway, got the usual
nine points of protection, naked AC:1, buffed
AC:-17.

T:7606, rats, lost both horses to the enemy; soldier
ants got the older one, recently advanced to a
horse, a black naga hatchling got the newer one,
still a pony. Bat Bait's revenge was swift in each
case, but still...

T:7964, Bat Bait drank an unidentified blessed
smokey potion from the altar heap in his player's
hopes of a wish for a bag of holding, instead, got
treated to hallucination, locked self in a room
alone until it wore off about 300 turns later.
Came out of the locked room, only immediately to
meet and tame a new pony, Whinney III.

T:8063, the Mordor orc in the nest of boulders
dead, and only five boulders intact, moved three
of them to plug holes in the temple wall. If ever
this altar gets converted, those will help keep
order among arriving monsters, except giants.

T:8251, rats! Noticed when descending to Mines 4
that I'd somehow lost a large cat, only to have
the other one disappear courtesy of a level
teleporter. Down to a large dog and a pony just
when Bat Bait needs troop strength to raid Mines
End.

T:8415, backtracked, luckily the level teleport
was upward, found original pet cat on Mines 2/4.
Back down to clean out Mines 4/6 and below. Bat
Bait needs to buff up dagger skills to have some
alternative besides the magic whistle to spell
casting, in case the pets get lunched soon.

T:9035, player needs head examined, managed to
whistle pony into a pit to its death, while
backtracking to Mines Town to retrieve forgotten
pick axe. Grrrr. Also pulled out candles, lamps,
lanterns, and all gems not identified as worthless
into a cursed sack, and left it on top of the altar
heap, making Bat Bait unburdened for the first time
in a long time. Heading back down to Mines End now,
prime YASD territory.

T:9421, yikes, Mines 6/8 is a bones level too, and
the ground around the foot of the stairs is littered
with corpses of nasties Bat Bait hasn't yet seen.
This could get ugly, time to go upstairs and rest to
recover full spell points. If what is in sight is
stuff the deceased PC _could_ handle, meeting what
it couldn't handle isn't going to evoke joy.

T:9706, while resting, met and tamed a large dog,
Barks A Lot IV. Killed a bat, see an orc caught in
a web Bat Bait also was trapped by, and an
approaching owl bear. Good time to practice up on
dagger skills.

T:10209, Bat Bait found a bag of holding on the
level a while back, which sure helps. Now, nearly
done exploring Mines 6/8, we find the reason for
the mess, HULKOR's ghost. In between, several winter
wolf cubs got in some real damage, and a Dwarf King,
Yeti, gargoyle, and other various monsters kept the
pot stirred. How strange, the ghost was not on its
gravestone nor did it have any possessions.

T:10246, found the gravesite, and it was the
gargoyle that did for our predecessor. From the
